KG42.register("clusters-fcb01c875fb339654083b1de",{"id":"04-energy_collectives::v142-d-K006","paper":"04-energy_collectives","label":"Geographical transaction costs and regional exchange balances across three neighborhoods","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K006","label":"Geographical transaction costs and regional exchange balances across three neighborhoods","market_meaning":"When the geographical preference model with three neighborhoods is adopted, the manager incorporates differentiated transaction costs based on exchange quantities on connecting lines and allocates community exchanges through neighborhood balance constraints. The N1 and N2 balances are currently retained, but the N3 gap means that the complete three-neighborhood allocation has not yet achieved closure.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM","LEM_DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The scope is the union of the original labels LEM in R013 and LEM_DEM in R016; the same Eq. (12) supports the linkage between their geographical branches, but these labels do not justify merging all local and regional markets. The references apply only to the three neighborhoods and introduce neither other objective branches nor guarantees for physical power flows.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Geographical costs and neighborhood energy balances jointly determine spatial allocation, with market significance independent of the largest-importer and intertemporal peak-shaving branches. Only the geographical branch of R013 is shared; the full set of interface models is not introduced merely because they involve the same manager.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R016","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the regional exchange costs and the frozen N1 and N2 balance constraints."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides only the geographical preference objective and the conditions for its selection by the manager; the same Eq. (12) is not counted again."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K006-C01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C007"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"The same geographical cost objective for three neighborhoods is assigned to the manager and regional allocation functions, respectively; this does not constitute two independent cost terms."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K006-C02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C007","v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-v"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C002","v141-c-R016::x::v141-c-R016-x-v"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"The line exchange quantities in the geographical objective also enter the neighborhood balances, coupling costs and spatial feasibility in the decision problem; the current connection covers only the frozen N1 and N2 conditions."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M01","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C007","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"The same geographical cost expression in the same three-neighborhood case, with only its display unified; regional balances are not a substitute for this repeated objective."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-v","v141-c-R016::x::v141-c-R016-x-v"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e09"],"rationale":"The source explicitly specifies the exchange vector formed by the same three connecting lines, retaining its cost and balance roles; the vector is not equated with the component for a single line."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-q-imp","v141-c-R016::x::v141-c-R016-x-qimp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"Corresponds to total imports only in the scalar geographical branch of Eq. (12), excluding the use of R013 for vectors across time periods."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-q-exp","v141-c-R016::x::v141-c-R016-x-qexp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"Corresponds to total exports only in the same geographical branch, retaining the original domain description."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::theta::v141-c-R013-th-gamma-geo","v141-c-R016::theta::v141-c-R016-theta-gamma-geo"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"The same vector of geographical transaction costs for the three lines; the correspondence is supported by the definition, rather than merely by identical symbols."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::theta::v141-c-R013-th-gamma-imp","v141-c-R016::theta::v141-c-R016-theta-gamma-imp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"Corresponds to the scalar import coefficient in Eq. (12), without generalizing to other temporal dimensions or case parameters."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-M07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::theta::v141-c-R013-th-gamma-exp","v141-c-R016::theta::v141-c-R016-theta-gamma-exp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"rationale":"Corresponds to the scalar export coefficient in Eq. (12); the local references in the two chains are retained separately."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The N3 balance in Eq. (12) in B repeats v_13; R016 therefore retains only N1 and N2. The existing chains are insufficient to confirm complete conservation across the three neighborhoods, and the third balance cannot be inferred and supplied automatically.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R016"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C007","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original N3 text and line directions, and have C supplement the balance after confirming the complete neighborhood partition and conservation; do not independently replace the repeated term with v_23 in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Line directions, exchange quantity units, feasible regions, and the signs of geographical weights have not been fully specified; relative transaction costs are also insufficient to demonstrate satisfaction of all physical power-flow or line-capacity constraints.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R016"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R016::x::v141-c-R016-x-qj","v141-c-R016::x::v141-c-R016-x-v","v141-c-R016::theta::v141-c-R016-theta-gamma-geo","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check variable domains, signs, units, and the conditions for preserving convexity; if physical network feasibility is required, source-supported network constraints are additionally needed and cannot be inferred from economic cost terms."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G03","category":"unverified_source","description":"The sources for the geographical objective, line definitions, and neighborhood balances are all unverified; the juxtaposition of the LEM and LEM_DEM labels does not mean that market classification approval has been completed in this round.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R016"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, manually check the figure, Eq. (12), and the scope classification, retaining the current original labels and the unresolved balance."}]},"rule_refs":["04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R016","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R013"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-cb8f993b6ad4c7bc","KG31-3fa7c9f6716d2240"]});
